Spec: Source Tree

Purpose:
  Contain the browser implementation for the TODO app.
  Preserve model, service, component, and bootstrap boundaries for source files.

Structure:
  ./src.sdd: Source-tree spec.
  ./models/: Domain models and colocated model specs.
  ./services/: Business logic, persistence adapters, and colocated service specs.
  ./components/: UI components and colocated component specs.
  ./index.html: Application entry point.
  ./main.js: Browser bootstrap that mounts @App into the DOM.
  ./components/*.sdd: Component-level SpecDD contracts.
  ./models/*.sdd: Model-level SpecDD contracts.
  ./services/*.sdd: Service-level SpecDD contracts.

Owns:
  Source-tree organization and implementation boundaries.
  ./src.sdd
  ./index.html
  ./main.js
  ./components/*.sdd
  ./models/*.sdd
  ./services/*.sdd

Can modify:
  ./src.sdd
  ./index.html
  ./main.js
  ./components/*.sdd
  ./models/*.sdd
  ./services/*.sdd

Can read:
  ./**
  ../tests/**

Must:
  Keep source organized into models, services, and components.
  Keep DOM manipulation inside components.
  Keep business logic inside services.
  Keep persistence access behind services.
  Keep browser bootstrap in ./main.js.
  Keep root component mounting in ./components/app.js.
  Use no inline JavaScript in ./index.html.
  Use inherited ES6 class-based architecture.

Must not:
  Put tests inside this source tree.
  Own repository-level app concerns outside the source tree.
